---
onetaskgraph_template: 1
description: >-
  A plan task's `## Budgets` section: every budget the task owns, in full. `plan-task`
  includes it after the task's `## Why`, and `just check-plan` renders it alone from the
  task's `orchestrator.budgets` metadata to hold the task's body to that record.
variables:
  # llmlint: ignore-block[contracts_have_one_source_or_a_drift_gate] The `budgets` description restates the shape `orchestrator/plan_budgets.py` states once, and `tests/test_plan_budgets_template.py` fails the moment the two part: the keys, the vocabularies and the name's cap are each compared with that module's own.
  budgets:
    description: >-
      One object per budget this task owns, or `[]` when it owns none, with exactly these
      keys. `id` (string, the budget's id in its budgets file). `name` (string, a short
      plain-English name on one line, at most 60 characters). `basis` (string, how solid
      the number is: `measured`, `arithmetic`, `design`, `published docs` or `estimate`).
      `repository` (string, the normalized origin `host/owner/name` of the repository the
      budget goes in). `file` (string, the repository-relative path of the `budgets.yaml`
      it goes in: `budgets.yaml` for a repo-wide budget, or a project's own file for a
      scoped one). `file_change` (string, `add`, `change` or `none`: what the task does
      to that file's entry). `measure` (string, what is measured, in words, as near as
      possible to where the product owner feels it). `inner_measure_reason` (string, why
      the measure is taken further inward than that, or `""` when it is not). `unit`
      (string), `direction` (string, `max` or `min`) and `threshold` (a finite number),
      each meaning what it means in onebudgetspec. `workload` (string, the realistic
      workload the threshold holds at, which is never written into the budgets file).
      `evidence` (string, where the number came from: a spike report's id and figures, or
      the measurement it rests on). `command` (string, the command that performs the
      measurement, as it will be registered). The same list is the task's
      `orchestrator.budgets` metadata. Newly authored records also have `schema_version`
      (integer literal 2), `source` (string, `direct` or `telemetry`) and
      `check_runtime_seconds` (finite number >= 0, excluding booleans). Direct executes
      the work/check it measures, including commands recording their result; telemetry
      reads existing timing/history records without executing measured work. Runtime
      estimates elapsed seconds of the entire command at the stated workload, including
      setup/reads, distinct from target, unit and basis. Evidence states the estimate's
      source. Never infer either field from basis or command. Exact legacy keys remain readable.
    type: list
    items: object
    default: []
  # llmlint: ignore-end[contracts_have_one_source_or_a_drift_gate]
---
{#-
  THE READERS. The worker this task dispatches, its judge, and a person following a design
  document's link to this section. The heading is exactly `## Budgets`, so the section's
  anchor is `budgets`; each budget's own heading is its name.
-#}
{% if budgets %}
## Budgets

{% for budget in budgets %}
{% if (budget.schema_version | default(0)) == 2 %}
<a id="{{ budget.id | e }}"></a>
{% endif %}
### {{ budget.name }}

- **Id:** `{{ budget.id }}`
- **Measure:** {{ budget.measure }}
{% if budget.inner_measure_reason %}
- **Inner measure, because:** {{ budget.inner_measure_reason }}
{% endif %}
- **Target:** {% if budget.direction == "max" %}at most{% elif budget.direction == "min" %}at least{% else %}{{ budget.direction }}{% endif %} {{ budget.threshold }} {{ budget.unit }}
- **Basis:** {{ budget.basis }}
{% if (budget.schema_version | default(0)) == 2 %}
- **Measurement source:** {{ budget.source }}
- **Check runtime:** approximately {{ budget.check_runtime_seconds }} seconds
{% endif %}
- **Workload:** {{ budget.workload }}
- **Evidence:** {{ budget.evidence }}
- **Command:** {% if "`" in budget.command %}{{ budget.command }}{% else %}`{{ budget.command }}`{% endif %}

- **Registered in:** `{{ budget.file }}` of `{{ budget.repository }}`, {% if budget.file_change == "add" %}an entry this task adds{% elif budget.file_change == "change" %}an entry this task changes{% elif budget.file_change == "none" %}an entry this task leaves as it is{% else %}{{ budget.file_change }}{% endif %}


{% endfor %}
{% endif %}
